    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d94">

                <pb facs="0176" n="144" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v06/pg144"/>

                <head>94. Telegram From the Embassy in Cuba to the Department of State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d94-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Havana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1958-07-11T02:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 11, 1958—2
                                a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>49. For Snow
                    ARA. During conference with Batista July 10 he stated he understood US
                    suspension of shipment of combat arms and our desire for non-involvement in
                    Cuban internal affairs. However, he was deeply concerned over what GOC considers as US intervention in Cuban affairs.
                    He has been informed by his Ambassadors in England and Canada that these nations
                    declined to sell arms to Cuba because US allegedly refused to give clearance. He
                    added that if GOC does not receive arms it could
                    bring about overthrow of Cuban Government.</p>
                <p>I said I was unaware of the foregoing and would advise my government of his
                    concern.</p>
                <p>Request information concerning validity of above.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d94-f2"
                    /></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
